WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:02.060
- What's up everybody, Dr. Mike here.

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:05.070
I'm incredibly excited to
announce that this week's video

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.930
is officially all natural.

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:08.300
Check this out!

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.330
Impressive right, and
you know what that means?

00:00:10.330 --> 00:00:11.163
No you don't.

00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:11.996
I don't either.

00:00:11.996 --> 00:00:12.829
Doesn't mean anything.

00:00:12.829 --> 00:00:15.400
This week I'm gonna be talking
about misleading food labels

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.900
and my top ten tips on how to
be a more educated consumer.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:19.837
Number 10.

00:00:19.837 --> 00:00:23.870
Don't buy into the meaningless phrases.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:26.410
All natural foods can
still contain chemicals.

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:29.120
Even the FDA website doesn't
have a formal definition

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.230
of all natural, plus, even if something

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.263
is fully all natural, it still
doesn't mean it's healthy.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:39.650
Your energy drink can contain
more caffeine than you think,

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:41.800
and that's courtesy of the guarana bean,

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.980
which contains two to
three times more caffeine

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.310
than the coffee bean, and
energy drink companies

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.350
don't have to add that to the
caffeine content on the can

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.500
because it's part of
their propriety blend.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:55.460
You see low fat on nutrition label,

00:00:55.460 --> 00:00:58.280
and you automatically
assume it must be healthy.

00:00:58.280 --> 00:01:01.430
First of all, you shouldn't
be so scared of dietary fat,

00:01:01.430 --> 00:01:03.540
and second of all, most of these companies

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.600
just jack up the sugar content

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:07.120
to make up for the lost taste.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:08.283
Not so healthy right?

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.460
Your bacon says no added nitrates,

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.940
it must be preservative free.

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:14.880
Not so fast.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:17.690
If it contains something
like celery root powder,

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.130
that's just another
form of added nitrates,

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.330
that's how they get you.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.750
Your food tastes really sweet,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.070
but the label says zero grams
of sugar, how's that possible?

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.500
Well it's likely that you're ingesting

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.820
artificial sweeteners like aspartame,

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:33.880
and while we don't have absolute evidence

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:36.540
that it's bad for your
health, what we do know now,

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:38.660
is it does change your brain chemistry

00:01:38.660 --> 00:01:41.340
and make you crave more unhealthy
foods throughout the day.

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.830
You're half way there
to the number one point

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:45.973
that will make you an educated consumer.

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:50.000
Zero grams of sugar added.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.130
It's a great thing,

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.490
but you still need to
check the nutrition facts

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:55.270
for the naturally occurring sugar.

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.430
For example, if you have
a cup of orange juice

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.510
in the morning made up of four oranges,

00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:01.990
that's 36 grams of sugar,

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:04.000
same as a Coke, but guess what,

00:02:04.000 --> 00:02:07.143
the label will still say
zero grams of added sugar.

00:02:09.180 --> 00:02:11.730
Don't fall for these
unsubstantiated health claims

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.720
you often find on food packaging.;

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.010
it boosts your immunity, it
helps your skin stay radiant.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:20.260
Most of these health claims
are often vague or exaggerated.

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.460
In fact, the Journal of
Nutrition Education and Behavior,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.590
found that these claims
appeared mostly on foods

00:02:25.590 --> 00:02:28.930
high in saturated fats, sugars, or sodium.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:31.870
Just stick to the nutrition
facts and the ingredient list.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.300
Also, be skeptical when
the packaging touts

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:35.810
a single ingredient.

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.860
Usually that's just a slight-of-hand move

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:40.060
to distract you from the
other unhealthy ingredients

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:40.933
found elsewhere.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:46.490
Whole wheat cereals, whole
wheat bars, whole wheat bread,

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:49.190
you think you're getting a
true whole wheat product?

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.360
Not so fast.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:52.280
You have to look at the first ingredient

00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:55.320
in the ingredient section,
which is the most abundant one,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.040
and it has to have the
word whole, in order for it

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.930
to be made predominantly of whole wheat.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.913
Number dos, va.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:06.780
Light, that sounds like a great quality

00:03:06.780 --> 00:03:08.400
for your food to have.

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.370
Light, means low in fat,
low in calories, right?

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.560
Not necessarily.

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:15.600
If a food tastes light,
if it's light in color,

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.810
it can still carry the light label.

00:03:17.810 --> 00:03:20.090
So don't get too excited
when you see light

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:21.350
in the title of your food.

00:03:21.350 --> 00:03:24.260
The number one tip,
yes the number one tip,

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:26.593
to make you an educated food consumer,

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:31.500
look at the serving size.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.660
I've made this mistake so many times.

00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:35.910
I've gotten a container
of soup, and I said oh,

00:03:35.910 --> 00:03:38.020
it has slightly more
sodium than I thought,

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:40.110
and then I ate it, and then I realized,

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.870
the serving size was a
quarter of the container,

00:03:42.870 --> 00:03:44.700
so that means I had four times

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.630
the amount of sodium I initially had.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.690
Now look, you get an ice cream container,

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:52.060
and it says, 120 calories per half a cup,

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:54.830
how many half a cup's are
in your bowl of ice cream.

00:03:54.830 --> 00:03:56.830
The FDA's even catching on to this one.

00:03:56.830 --> 00:04:00.330
If the entire container's likely
to be eaten in one sitting,

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:01.920
the companies will be obligated

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.740
to put the entire container
as a serving size.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:05.750
So there you have it.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.320
You are now an educated food consumer.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:10.330
Please don't stress
about your food choices,

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:12.430
because stress is a true killer.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:15.780
Be smart, educate yourself,
know what you put in your body,

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.693
and stay healthy, thanks for watching.

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.780
Seven, your bacon's (laughs).

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:24.850
Well guess what, why do I
keep saying well guess what?

00:04:24.850 --> 00:04:27.157
Number nine, why am I doing six (laughs).

00:04:29.018 --> 00:04:31.601
(upbeat music)

